We started by cleaning and preparing two datasets: trading data and sentiment data.
The timestamp column in the trading dataset required careful preprocessing due to format inconsistencies, which were resolved by applying appropriate datetime parsing techniques.
Both datasets were aligned at a daily level by extracting the date component and merging them using a common date key. This ensured that each trade was mapped to the corresponding market sentiment.
Next, we engineered key behavioral metrics such as daily PnL, win rate, trade frequency, average trade size, and long/short ratio. These metrics were aggregated by sentiment classification to analyze how trader performance varies across different emotional market states.
Finally, we visualized the results using bar charts to compare performance and behavior across sentiment categories.
